.TH sum "" "Command"
.SH NAME
sum \- print checksum of a file
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBsum [\fIfile ...\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.HS
sum -- print checksum of a file
Usage:	sum [ file ... ]
.HE
.B sum
reads each
.IR file ,
or the standard input if none is given, and prints an unsigned
checksum together with the size of the file in 512-byte blocks,
rounded up.
If more than one
.I file
is given,
.B sum
also prints the file's name.
.PP
The checksum is simply the sum, modulo 65536, of every byte read.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.B cmp
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
.B sum
reports an error and goes on to the next
.I file
if a named file cannot be opened or a read error occurs; its exit
status is nonzero if any file could not be summed.
